{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>Of Zerah.</b> He is צֹחַר — a term of צֹהַר. But the clan of Ohad disappeared, and likewise five clans of the tribe of Benjamin — for he descended to Egypt with ten sons, yet here he counted only five. And likewise Ezbon of Gad — here are seven clans (Tanchuma). And I found in the Talmud Yerushalmi: when Aharon died, the clouds of glory departed, and the Canaanites came to wage war against Israel, and they set their hearts to return to Egypt, and they went back eight stages — from Mount Hor to Moserah — as it says ״וּבְנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל נָסְעוּ מִבְּאֵרֹת בְּנֵי יַעֲקָן מוֹסֵרָה שָׁם מֵת אַהֲרֹן״ (Deuteronomy 10). But did he not die at Mount Hor, and from Moserah to Mount Hor there are eight stages going forward? Rather, they went back, and the sons of Levi pursued them to bring them back, and [the others] killed from among them seven clans, and from the sons of Levi fell four clans: the clan of Shimi and the Uzieli clan, and of the sons of Yitzhar none were counted here except the Korchi clan, and the fourth I do not know what it is (Talmud Yerushalmi Sotah 1). And Rabbi Tanchuma interpreted that they died in the plague at the counsel of Bilaam. But according to the deficit missing from the tribe of Shimon in this census compared to the first census at the wilderness of Sinai, it appears that all 24,000 fell from the tribe of Shimon."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:12:54.999819108Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}